<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12358" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dāvīd</span></b> , m.
		indecl., or vīdis (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>gen.</i> David,
				<i><span class="en">Aus. Ephem. 3, 84</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Davidis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juvenc. 1, 151</span></i>
			; acc. -vīda,
				<i><span class="en">Juvenc. 2, 577</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">David,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					2 Reg. 23, 16</span></i>
			), <i>the second king of the Jews, and principal
				author of the Book of Psalms</i>, <i><span class="en">Tert.
				adv. Jud. 9</span></i> et 12; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Ruth 4,
				17</span></i> et saep.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dāvīdĭcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to David</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sedul. Carm. 4, 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lyra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var. 2, 20</span></i>
			.</div>
